I'm currently considering making a patch which always players to see
the weight of identified items. But rather than using the abstract
weight units used by the game, I figure it would be nicer to come up
with a conversation to real-life weight units. So I was just browsing
this: http://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Weight and thinking about what the
conversion should be.

I've decided that 1 nethack weight unit is around about 40 grams. This
means a longsword weighs 1.6kg, a food ration 800g, and a human around
58kg. The human is a bit too light, but I think it's close enough...
especially considering that rings would weigh 120g and amulets 800g!
Can you imagine how big those things must be? No wonder you can only
wear one ring on each hand; and damn it must be uncomfortable to wear
one of those amulets.

So maybe a conversion of 1 unit -> 50 grams would be better for the
weight of a human and for a couple of other things, but it would make
the weights of some of the small stuff even more ridiculous. Just
imagine throwing a 500g "tripe ration" to your pet cat, who then
catches it. I can tell you, if I threw something that big to my cat,
the cat would run away!

Incidentally, do you think it's a good idea to be able to see the
weight of identified items?


